WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.826
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.126 --> 00:00:09.501
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:16.238
Unit twelve: Formal Academic Style. Today you will write in a formal, objective academic tone.

4
00:00:16.538 --> 00:00:19.167
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.424
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.075
Formal.

7
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:28.721
Formal means serious and correct in style.

8
00:00:29.317 --> 00:00:30.863
Use formal language.

9
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.288
Your turn. Say: Formal.

10
00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:37.995
Formal.

11
00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:39.705
Objective.

12
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:43.796
Objective means based on facts, not feelings.

13
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:45.721
Stay objective.

14
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:49.236
Your turn. Say: Objective.

15
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.217
Objective.

16
00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:54.683
Tone.

17
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:57.613
Tone means the attitude in writing.

18
00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:59.659
Keep a neutral tone.

19
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.717
Your turn. Say: Tone.

20
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:06.336
Tone.

21
00:01:07.083 --> 00:01:08.189
Contraction.

22
00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:11.531
Contraction means a short form like don't.

23
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:13.791
Avoid contractions.

24
00:01:14.383 --> 00:01:17.105
Your turn. Say: Contraction.

25
00:01:19.967 --> 00:01:21.014
Contraction.

26
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:22.844
Colloquial.

27
00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.384
Colloquial means used in casual speech.

28
00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:28.844
Avoid colloquial words.

29
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:32.056
Your turn. Say: Colloquial.

30
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.064
Colloquial.

31
00:01:36.817 --> 00:01:37.528
Hedge.

32
00:01:38.517 --> 00:01:40.725
Hedge means to make a claim less strong.

33
00:01:41.317 --> 00:01:42.608
Hedge your claim.

34
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:45.753
Your turn. Say: Hedge.

35
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.462
Hedge.

36
00:01:50.217 --> 00:01:51.206
Passive.

37
00:01:52.217 --> 00:01:54.518
Passive means focusing on the action.

38
00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:56.849
The passive sounds formal.

39
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:59.998
Your turn. Say: Passive.

40
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:03.660
Passive.

41
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.557
Concise.

42
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.515
Concise means short and clear.

43
00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:10.362
Be concise.

44
00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.417
Your turn. Say: Concise.

45
00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:17.407
Concise.

46
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.187
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:25.050
Visal, what makes writing formal?

48
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:37.080
Avoid contractions, slang and personal phrases such as I think. Use precise vocabulary and full forms, such as do not instead of don't.

49
00:02:38.183 --> 00:02:39.718
Why is the passive used?

50
00:02:40.817 --> 00:02:51.445
The passive focuses on the action, not the person, so it sounds objective. For example, the experiment was repeated three times.

51
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:53.563
What is hedging?

52
00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:04.152
Hedging makes a claim careful, using words such as may, might, seems and tends to. It shows that you are not claiming absolute truth.

53
00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.893
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.609
Grammar focus: Formal alternatives.

55
00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:12.049
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.924
a lot of becomes a large number of.

57
00:03:15.817 --> 00:03:17.770
get becomes obtain or receive.

58
00:03:18.733 --> 00:03:25.830
Replace informal words with formal ones: a lot of becomes many or a large number of, get becomes obtain and kids becomes children.

59
00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:30.292
Be careful! Don't say: Kids is very important.

60
00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:34.616
Say: Children are very important.

61
00:03:34.916 --> 00:03:36.590
Use a plural verb.

62
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.145
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:42.085
Making It Formal.

64
00:03:42.385 --> 00:03:44.838
Makara reads her first draft again.

65
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:49.389
It has contractions and informal words such as kids and stuff.

66
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:52.992
She changes them to children and materials.

67
00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.835
She uses the passive and a hedge such as may.

68
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:00.297
Her tutor says the style is now suitable.

69
00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:05.692
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.329
Formal writing avoids blank.

71
00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:12.898
A, contractions. B, nouns. C, full stops.

72
00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:19.118
The answer is A: contractions.

73
00:04:20.283 --> 00:04:22.387
Objective means based on blank.

74
00:04:22.687 --> 00:04:26.039
A, luck. B, facts. C, moods.

75
00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.565
The answer is B: facts.

76
00:04:32.717 --> 00:04:34.101
May is a blank word.

77
00:04:34.401 --> 00:04:37.381
A, rude. B, funny. C, hedging.

78
00:04:40.933 --> 00:04:42.759
The answer is C: hedging.

79
00:04:43.917 --> 00:04:45.777
Concise means short and blank.

80
00:04:46.077 --> 00:04:49.881
A, clear. B, wrong. C, loud.

81
00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:55.468
The answer is A: clear.

82
00:04:56.617 --> 00:04:58.663
What does Makara change kids to?

83
00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:02.337
A, friends. B, children. C, kiddos.

84
00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.190
The answer is B: children.

85
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:12.900
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.250
What makes writing formal?

87
00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.481
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:25.781 --> 00:05:39.999
Formal writing avoids contractions, slang and personal phrases. It uses precise vocabulary, the passive voice and careful words such as may or tends to. It stays objective and concise.

89
00:05:40.299 --> 00:05:41.962
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:47.128
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and formal alternatives.

91
00:05:47.428 --> 00:05:52.808
Today's value is professionalism. Be prepared, polite and reliable in everything you do.

92
00:05:53.108 --> 00:05:55.935
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:56.235 --> 00:05:58.945
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

